.aider*
*.prt

# ── EXTERNAL DIFFERENTIAL CORPUS (plan §11 A4 / P14 Step 13) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚖ LICENSING (load-bearing — do NOT relax): GnuCOBOL and its testsuite are GPL-3.0; this repo is BSL 1.1.
# Their test TEXT is NEVER committed here. It is fetched on demand by scripts/fetch-gnucobol-tests.ps1 into
# this ignored tree. What we DO commit is ours alone: the retrieval script, the .at extractor, the adapter
# test project, and tests/external/gnucobol-expectations.json (independently-authored FACTS about cases —
# per-case classification + our §-cited rationale — never their source or their expected text).
tests/external/gnucobol/
tests/external/*.tar.*
tests/external/*.7z
tests/external/*.zip
# WHERE THE LINE SITS (owner decision 2026-07-19): the substantial expressive content — their COBOL test
# SOURCE and their EXPECTED OUTPUT text — is never committed. Short factual GROUP TITLES and KEYWORDS are
# citable identification (the same nominative use an article describing the suite would make), so the
# differential report and the expectations ledger MAY carry them. Case IDs ("syn_move:38") are coordinates
# we compute. Net effect: our reports are committable; their corpus is not.
scripts/__pycache__/
# Regenerable output of scripts/gnucobol_differential.py (re-run to recreate). NOT a licensing
# exclusion — per the owner's 2026-07-19 ruling its case titles/keywords are citable; it is simply
# generated. The COMMITTED artifact is tests/external/gnucobol-expectations.json (our classifications).
tests/external/gnucobol-differential-report.json

# Session convenience files — untracked by convention (feedback_plans_in_repo)
/scratchpad/

# ── Obsidian vault (notes under kb/) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The NOTES under kb/ ARE tracked — a derived, cross-linked knowledge base (see docs/DOC_INDEX.md
# "Derived knowledge base"). Only Obsidian's per-user / volatile state is ignored so pane moves, caches, and
# vendored plugin code don't churn the repo. community-plugins.json (the plugin LIST) stays tracked for reinstall.
# (VAULT/ retired 2026-07-23 — notes relocated to kb/; only the repo-root .obsidian/ rules below apply)

# Obsidian config at the REPO ROOT (vault root became the repo on 2026-07-23 — one vault over the whole project).
# ⛔ NEVER commit the Local REST API key/cert (data.json) or volatile state. community-plugins.json (the plugin LIST,
# at .obsidian/ top level) MAY be committed for reinstall. The generated code-reference notes are a build output.
.obsidian/*
!.obsidian/app.json
!.obsidian/community-plugins.json
.trash/

# Generated code-reference notes (a build output — regenerated from src/ by the vault generator).
kb/Reference/
